 # Changelog
 
 Dated, factual, one line per change. Newest first.
+
+## 2026-11-12 - Phase 4, Block F (sign-offs, twin tax, statute and levy check, figures, pipeline integrity, outsider reproducibility)
+- F0: the sign-off session is recorded: the 22 RETIRE rows are retired and their code removed (trust-penalty logic, school-curriculum and social-norm state of the twin, the cost-benefit and optimiser blocks and the 17 `interventions.*` constants; `intervention_figures` of the dashboard data layer); the 54 SIGN rows carry `john_signoff = approved (John, 2026-11-12)` (including `twin.mm.penetration_cap`); new register column `label`; `feeds` descriptions read the current values through a token (`{FIG51}`); no unsigned ASSUMPTION / UNKNOWN row feeds a published claim except the new levy lever; C062 is no longer BLOCKED. Register: 205 rows (ASSUMPTION 66, UNKNOWN 9, DATA 29, CALIBRATED 3, RETIRED 98). Removing the trust penalty (it did bind in the old-model reference used by the E2.3 conversion) moved the morale odds ratios by -2 to -4% and Fig 5.1 (combined 11.26% -> 10.17%, naive sum 13.07% -> 12.0%).
+- F1: `base.personal_income_tax_rate` (15%) and `base.presumptive_tax_rate` (3%) are RETIRED: new taxpayers' tax is the statutory schedule applied to the DISTRIBUTION of ILFS 2024 earnings (100 quantile cells; `src/04_models/statutory_tax.py`, `data/processed/twin_inputs.json tax_base_cells`): TZS 407,215 per informal earner, an effective average rate of 10.4% of mean earnings; TZS 729,529 per household enterprise (3.56% of mean turnover). The agent simulation applies the schedule to each agent's own earnings. Twin year 10: baseline 13.33% (was 13.80%), policy 15.44% (was 16.69%).
+- F2: schedules checked against the Finance Acts 2024, 2025 and 2026: the resident schedule is unchanged; the presumptive schedule of the Finance Act 2026 (ceiling TZS 200M, 4.0% above TZS 11M, nil for 12 months for a new TIN starting a business: sensitivity only) is used. Mobile-money levy documented in `docs/mobile_money_levy.md` (National Payment Systems Act Cap. 437 s. 46A via the Finance Act 2021; tiered fixed fee; withdrawals only since 1 July 2023; GN 478V, GN 596C); the twin lever is now `twin.policy.hypothetical_additional_levy` (no effective rate of the current levy could be derived; unsigned). 9 documents added to `data/raw/SOURCES.csv`.
+- F3: persistence 0.75 (signed-off distribution, mode 0.75) beside 0.90 and 0.95 for 10 and 20 years, per stage and for the portfolio without Asset (`stage_economics.json persistence_sensitivity`, extra columns of `table40_stage_economics.csv`; portfolio ROI 20 years 3.64 / 3.89 / 6.94 / 9.04x; 10-year headline 3.23x).
+- F4: `src/06_figures/` (9 figures, one script each, PNG + SVG, byte-reproducible, run by `run_all.py`); `run_all.py --screenshots` (Playwright); `docs/interventions.yaml` (draft) replaces the frozen LLM sections as the registrar's input (`outputs/frozen` -> `_archive/frozen`; the register has 6 entries); `src/imported/` -> `_archive/imported/`; typed macro and stage values removed from `shared_context.py` and `Home.py`.
+- F5: README, LICENSE (MIT; CC BY 4.0 note), CITATION.cff, `data/processed/README.md`, final `docs/claims_map.csv` (draft in `_archive/`); tests that need restricted raw data skip with a message; `run_all.py --from-processed` runs without the microdata (`data/processed/ilfs_tax_base.json`); outsider simulation done.
+- Tests: `test_statutory_tax.py`, `test_figures.py`, `test_interventions_yaml.py`, `test_docs_and_portability.py` (new); `conftest.py`, `test_assumptions.py`, `test_agent_odds_ratios.py`, `test_digital_twin.py`, `test_register.py`, `test_from_processed.py`, `test_stage_economics.py` updated.
 
 ## 2026-11-12 - Phase 4, Block E3 (agent model harmonised with the morale model, twin fix, Table 40 revisions, sign-off sheet)
 - E3.1: the agent and tier simulations use the tax-morale model's mechanism: interventions (USSD TIN nudge for mobile-money users, civic tax education for urban adults 18+) multiply each agent's yearly registration ODDS by the model's odds ratios (1.243, 1.304; 1.336 for agents reached by both, by the model's combination rule: driver deltas summed after x `tax_morale.combined_discount`). The trust / morale uplift path and the community-norm feedback are retired: 7 constants (agents.ussd.*, agents.edu.morale_uplift_*, agents.norm_uplift_factor) RETIRED, reason 'replaced by morale-model odds ratios (E3.1)'. The no-intervention path changed, so the E2.4 calibration was re-run (same target and method): conversion 0.0069, intercept -0.251, RMSE 0.228 pp, correlation -0.99; identified combination conversion x (mean index + intercept) = 0.332% a year. Year-10 registration 7.67% with the interventions vs 6.98% without (effect 0.69 pp; was +0.30 pp); tier year 10: 92.3 / 0.2 / 0.9 / 2.0 / 1.8 / 2.8%. C062 is still BLOCKED by the four agents.p_comply weights.
