+twin,twin.policy.hypothetical_additional_levy,0.003,ASSUMPTION,"Policy scenario: a HYPOTHETICAL ADDITIONAL levy of 0.3% of the value of mobile-money payments (the twin's mobile_money_gdp_pct x GDP), on top of the levy that already exists. Context (Block F2, docs/mobile_money_levy.md): Tanzania already levies mobile-money transactions under section 46A of the National Payment Systems Act (Cap. 437), a TIERED FIXED FEE per transaction (TZS 10 to TZS 2,000 by value band, GN 596C of 5 October 2022), on cash WITHDRAWALS ONLY since the Finance Act 2023 (1 July 2023); its revenue is already inside the observed tax-to-GDP baseline. No collection figure for the current levy was found, so no effective rate (collections / transaction value) could be derived for it and the lever is not expressed as a change relative to it. The only published collection estimate is for the earlier regime (GSMA: TZS 252 billion in 2022 on BoT mobile payments of TZS 114.3 trillion, about 0.22%, transfers and withdrawals). The 0.3% is a scenario input with no evidence behind it.",C079 (Fig 5.2 digital twin),no,<=5% (max change 0.4% in policy_final_tax_to_gdp_pct),SIGN as is,Design choice; no data bear on it. Sensitivity (+/-20%): <=5% (max change 0.4% in policy_final_tax_to_gdp_pct).,published
